<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n16906" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀσχημάτιστος</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μᾰ],
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>without form</i> or
				<i>figure,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Phdr.</u>
				247c
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Ph.</u>
				191a2
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>that cannot be represented by a figure, Theol. Ar.</i><i><span class="en">
				11
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> Astrol.,
				<i>not in aspect with</i> other planets, Vett. Val.<i><span class="en">
				102.8
			</span></i>, Anon.in <i><span class="en">
				Ptol.
				<u>Tetr.</u>
				104
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>not employing figures of speech,</i> of orators, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.835b
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φράσις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.H.
					<u>Pomp.</u>
					5
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Demetr.
				<u>Eloc.</u>
				67
			</span></i>. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-τως</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.H.
					<u>Rh.</u>
					10.11
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
